Kamalie enemies weapons and builds (@kamalie-builds: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @ws-kamalie-games) {
## Desired system

Levels, enemy types and weapons are generated from authored constraints and physical mechanics. The designer builds the rules for randomness and the vocabulary of parts and expressions. Builds are assembled during a run from found objects. Skill, experimentation and the player's knowledge persist; powerups do not.

The first slice supplies sticks and bushes to prove the physical vocabulary. It does not imply implemented enemies, loot tables, death or a complete dungeon-crawler progression loop.

## Planned work

- [x] Generate weapon length and shape within playable material constraints.
- [ ] Generate compatible combinations of responsive and passive weapon parts.
- [ ] Generate enemies from body shapes, movement policies and physical expressions.
- [ ] Define bounded enemy perception and steering in the generated dungeon.
- [ ] Make enemy damage use the same local material/contact system.
- [ ] Define player damage and death without a HUD.
- [ ] Generate level encounter compositions from validated weighted definitions.
- [ ] Define drop occurrence separately from weighted item-family selection.
- [ ] Test several builds that differ mechanically rather than only numerically.
- [ ] Verify a fresh run inherits no mechanical advantage from a previous run.
}
